{
  "subject_sha": "34c865233df53a3930f29c8b7befc02208588d64",
  "verdict": "changes-requested",
  "summary": "Read-only review of PR #483 (batch bug-batch-432: #432, #441, #442, #460, #463, #464, #467) at 34c865233. The worktree HEAD matches. No code changed between the QA3 source checkpoint 938ae9c44 and 34c865233 (empty non-artifact diff), so the evidence recorded against 938ae9c44 applies to this SHA. Hosted checks are green on 34c865233. This PR has no earlier review findings; the only earlier attempt (round 1) produced no report.\n\nWhat is solid:\n- #464: facilityClock uses Europe/Rome through Intl. It is shared by dayKey, nowMinutes, overdueConsegne and findTherapiesDue. Pure tests cover midnight, the year boundary and both DST transitions with correct expected values, and a DB test covers 08:00 not overdue / 00:45 due / 00:46 overdue.\n- #460: the receipt table is additive (composite PK actorId+requestId, patient FK with cascade, no backfill) and its migration sorts after base. The receipt is written in the same SERIALIZABLE transaction as the clinical record. The payload hash rejects a reused requestId with a different body. Replay re-checks patient scope. P2002/P2034 are retried a bounded number of times. The concurrency and replay DB tests make meaningful assertions.\n- #467: a one-off is matched for the whole day instead of by band, in the writer, the feed, the exact summary and the due query.\n- #463: catalog status is read before per-name searches, the 'source unavailable' state stays distinct from 'not found', and the rate limit is unchanged.\n- #442: the barrier and bounded cleanup were reworked and checked by independent QA.\n- #432: pagination now fails closed on short, inconsistent or other-patient pages.\n\nTwo clinical regressions or gaps block approval:\n1. The giro and cartella client now sends expectedStato='da_erogare' on every write. This breaks the existing 'Somministra ora' correction for today's refused doses, which now always gets 409.\n2. #441: a one-off whose time is missing, unpadded or contradicted by a schedule is now dropped from the feed, the summary and the assistant without any 'to verify' surface. This includes legacy one-offs that had band flags and were visible before, and intake one-offs saved with an unpadded H:MM. That contradicts #441 ('restano da verificare') and #432 (no silent loss).\n\nEvidence notes:\n- Evidence for #441 reuses the #432 trace and video (identical hashes); only the screenshot is specific to #441.\n- The manifests reference checkpoint 938ae9c44, not 34c865233.\n- The packet's own Final Decision is PARTIAL: external review, migration before deployment and the demo deployment are still pending.\n- No evidence exercises 'Somministra ora' on a refused dose.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "frontend/src/lib/therapyAdministrationWrite.ts",
      "line": 57,
      "problem": "administrationBody now sends expectedStato:'da_erogare' unconditionally. PatientTherapySlotDetail's 'Somministra ora' action (administerAgain, frontend/src/components/operator/cartella/PatientTherapySlotDetail.tsx:129) re-administers today's doses already marked non_erogata through the same recordAdministration path. The server (backend/src/therapies/administration-record.ts) now answers 409 'La dose non è più da erogare' whenever an existing record's stato differs from expectedStato. The explicit refusal-to-given correction, which #460 says must remain a separate action, is therefore always rejected. Before this PR it worked.",
      "requested_change": "Send expectedStato only for pending-dose actions. Make the explicit correction path (administerAgain / missedToday) omit it, or send a distinct expected state such as 'non_erogata' that the server validates, so a correction still cannot overwrite an outcome it did not see. Keep the giro, Turno and assistant pending actions on 'da_erogare'.",
      "test_expectation": "Unit test: the body built for 'Somministra ora' on a not_administered dose does not carry expectedStato='da_erogare'. DB/HTTP test: refused dose, then correction via the client body, gives 200 and exactly one record now 'erogata'. A pending-only confirm still gets 409. Browser evidence on the final SHA: refuse, 'Somministra ora', reload shows Erogata."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "backend/src/therapies/slot-scheduling.ts",
      "line": 16,
      "problem": "oneTimeSlot/therapyBandEnabled, and the SQL twin therapyBandEnabledSql (backend/src/therapies/therapy-query.ts:6-10), make any una_tantum whose orarioSomministrazione is null, not strictly HH:MM, or different from a TherapySchedule.time invisible in every band. Such a dose disappears from the feed, the exact summary and the assistant due queue, and nothing marks it as 'da verificare'. Affected data includes legacy one-offs created through POST/PUT /patients/:id/therapies without a time but with band flags (visible before this PR), and intake one-offs: confirm-therapies.ts:77 accepts '8:30' and stores it unnormalized. The new test explicitly asserts that the null and '99:00' rows are absent. #441 requires contradictory clocks/schedules to stay 'da verificare', and #432 forbids silent loss of prescribed drugs.",
      "requested_change": "Keep writes rejected for invalid or contradictory one-offs. Do not drop them from reads: surface them in the feed and summary as a non-administrable 'da verificare' item, with no invented time, fascia or quantity, and count them in the assistant. Accept the zero-padding-equivalent H:MM form ('8:30' equals '08:30', the same value, as the diary already normalizes), or normalize it at intake confirmation. Apply the same rule in the TS and SQL implementations.",
      "test_expectation": "DB test: a una_tantum with null time and fasceMattina=true, one with '8:30', and one whose schedule time contradicts orarioSomministrazione all appear on the date as read-only 'to verify' (or, for '8:30', as a normal 08:30 dose). Summary totals and the assistant reflect them. Confirm/not-administered on the invalid ones returns 409/404 and creates no record."
    }
  ]
}

